  "summary": "The loopsy CLI includes daemon lifecycle commands (init, start, stop, status, doctor, enable/disable), phone pairing and revocation, relay reconfiguration, log viewing, and API-key show/rotate commands. When wired into an agent, the Loopsy MCP server exposes tools for peer listing, remote command execution, long-lived PTY sessions, file transfer, a shared key/value context store, messaging with ACKs, and read receipts.",
